  <processInformation>
    <dataSetInformation>
      <common:UUID>7252a0b3-9db5-4acc-99e5-fcfaa740af71</common:UUID>
      <name>
        <baseName xml:lang="en">Metal Building end-of-life, selective demolition, Lombardy Region</baseName>
      </name>
      <common:synonyms>Demolizione Selettiva / Decostruzione, edifici in metallo.</common:synonyms>
      <classificationInformation>
        <common:classification name="ILCDCategories" classes="../ILCDClassification.xml">
          <common:class level="0">Systems</common:class>
          <common:class level="1">Construction</common:class>
        </common:classification>
      </classificationInformation>
      <common:generalComment>Dataset developed within the ARCADIA project in the context of the Ph.D. of Federica Carollo (Politecnico di Milano). 
The dataset refers to the selective 1 m3 demolition of a commercial metal building that has a total volume (empty to full) of 80,000 m3.  
The dataset is composed of 7-unit processes:  
 
Input: 
1) Diesel consumption for the machinery use; 
2) Electricity consumption for the machinery use; 
3) Water consumption for the machinery use; 
4) Transport: Iron and Steel to Recycling; 
5) Transport of the Mixed C&amp;D to Recycling; 
Output: 
6) Recycling of EWC 17 09 04 - Mixed C&amp;D (Process: Mixed C&amp;D, recycling); 
7) Recycling of EWC 17 04 05 – Iron and Steel (Process: Iron and Steel, recycling).</common:generalComment>
      <referenceToExternalDocumentation type="source data set" refObjectId="ca1c1f2a-d734-4656-9fdf-437a353e27db" version="01.00.000" uri="../sources/ca1c1f2a-d734-4656-9fdf-437a353e27db.xml">
        <common:shortDescription>Carollo F. (2023). Circularity in construction and demolition waste management chain, Ph.D. Dissertation (Tutored by Rigamonti L., Ceruti F.). Politecnico di Milano. Background datasets from the EcoInvent database cut-off (v. 3.8) were used for the LCA study. </common:shortDescription>
      </referenceToExternalDocumentation>
    </dataSetInformation>
    <quantitativeReference type="Reference flow(s)">
      <referenceToReferenceFlow>0</referenceToReferenceFlow>
    </quantitativeReference>
    <time>
      <common:referenceYear>2022</common:referenceYear>
